{"sru": [{"id": "Sru", "headword": "श्रु", "headword_slp1": "Sru", "fold": "sru", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "capeller-sanskrit-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "श्रु श्रृणो॑ति श्रृणुते॑ pp. श्रुत॑ (q.v.) hear, learn\n(acc.) from (gen., abl., instr., & मुखात् or श्रकाशात्);\n hear — to\nbe (2 acc.);\n listen or give ear to (acc. of th. or gen. of pers.);\n hear\na teacher i.e. learn, study. M.P. be heard of, be known as or to be (2\nnom.);\n be studied, taught, or read. C. श्रव॑यति & शाव॑यति (˚ते)\ncause a person to hear, i.e. address, inform of, communicate to, tell\n(acc. of thing & acc., gen., or dat. of pers.);\n let hear i.e. proclaim,\nannounce, recite. D. श्रु॑शूषते (˚ति) wish or like to hear i.e. attend\nto, obey, wait on, serve (acc.). — अति M. be heard of i.e. be\ncelebrated above (all). अनु hear or learn (again);\n C. relate, tell (2\nacc.);\n D.M. obey. अभि hear, learn — to be (2 acc.). C. cause to\nhear, speak to, address (acc.). आ listen to (acc. of th., gen. or dat.\nof pers.);\n hear, learn;\n promise. C. proclaim, make known;\n address,\ninvoke, summon. अभ्या C. address. उप listen to (acc. or gen.),\nhear, learn from (मुखात् or सकाशात्), hear that — is (2 acc.).\nसमुप hear, listen to (acc. or gen.), learn from (abl.). परि hear,\nlearn, understand that—is (2 acc.). प्र M. be heard;\n become known or\nfamous. प्रति listen or give ear;\n say yes, promise. C. answer. वि\nhear, learn;\n P. be heard of, become known or famous. C. let hear,\nannounce, proclaim, tell;\n make known or famous, make resound. सम् hear\n(मुखात्), listen\n[]\nto (acc.);\n accede to the request of, make a\npromise to (loc. or dat.). C. let hear, announce, proclaim;\n make\nresound. अभिसम् hear, learn. प्रतिसम् make a promise to (gen.). —\nCf. अभिविशुत, अभिशुत॑, आशुत, परिशुत, वि॑शुत.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}, {"id": "sru", "headword": "स्रु", "headword_slp1": "sru", "fold": "sru", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "capeller-sanskrit-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "स्रु स्र॑वति (स्र॑व˚ते), pp. स्रुत flow, stream;\n flow\nwith (instr. or acc.);\n drip, leak (vessel);\n flow or waste away, perish,\nbe lost. C. स्रावयति & स्रवयति cause to flow, spill, shed. — अति\nflow over. अधि flow off (abl.). अभि flow hither. अव flow down;\nC. = अन्वव C. cause to flow down. आ & उप flow towards (acc.).\nनि flow down. निस् flow asunder or out, flow forth, rise from (abl).\nपरि flow around or abundantly;\n run away, pass (time). प्र flow\nforth, stream from (abl.);\n let\n[]\nflow, discharge. अभिप्र &\nसंप्र stream forth. वि stream forth, flow from (abl.);\n let flow,\ndischarge;\n melt away, perish. सम् flow or run together.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["स्रुः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["sruH"]}], "srut": [{"id": "Srut", "headword": "श्रुत्", "headword_slp1": "Srut", "fold": "srut", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "capeller-sanskrit-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "श्रुत् (—˚) hearing.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}, {"id": "srut", "headword": "स्रुत्", "headword_slp1": "srut", "fold": "srut", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "capeller-sanskrit-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "स्रुत् (—˚) flowing with, discharging.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "sruta": [{"id": "Sruta", "headword": "श्रुत", "headword_slp1": "Sruta", "fold": "sruta", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "capeller-sanskrit-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "श्रुत॑ a. heard, learnt, mentioned, stated, named, known as,\nfamous, celebrated;\n n. hearing, learning, lore, tradition, (sacred)\nknowledge.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["श्रुतं", "श्रुतः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["SrutaM", "SrutaH"]}], "srutakarman": [{"id": "Srutakarman", "headword": "श्रुतकर्मन्", "headword_slp1": "Srutakarman", "fold": "srutakarman", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "capeller-sanskrit-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "श्रुतकर्मन् m. N. of a hero (lit. of celebrated\ndeeds).", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "srutakama": [{"id": "SrutakAma", "headword": "श्रुतकाम", "headword_slp1": "SrutakAma", "